Package: lofi
Version: @VERSION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Essential: no
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Maintainer: Lofi <lofi@example.com>
Depends: ffmpeg, libopus0, ca-certificates
Recommends: libnss3
Suggests: yt-dlp
Homepage: https://github.com/mob5824m-wq/Discord-lofi
Description: Discord bot that plays lofi in a voice channel, with a web dashboard
 Lofi joins a voice channel in your Discord server and plays lofi without
 stopping, and serves a token-authenticated web dashboard to control it.
 .
 It can stream from YouTube broadcasts and SomaFM radio, shuffle your own
 music/ folder, or render Studio Lofi beats locally with no network at all.
 .
 This package installs the single-file `lofi` binary to /usr/local/bin and a
 systemd unit (not enabled) to /lib/systemd/system/lofi.service.
 .
 No bot token is shipped: set LOFI_TOKEN in /etc/lofi/lofi.env, or export it in
 your shell, then run `lofi --check` before starting the bot.
